NAME
    cat - print a file's contents

SYNOPSIS
    cat <path>...

DESCRIPTION
    Prints one or more real files' contents, concatenated in the order
    given, walled to the project's own directory tree (see 'cd'). With no
    <path> at all, passes piped stdin straight through unchanged instead -
    the classic 'cat' idiom for previewing a pipeline mid-stage - rather
    than erroring for a missing argument.

EXAMPLES
    cat notes.txt
    watch log 1 | cat
